# =====================================================================================
# .gitignore - files git should NOT track
#
# Two rules of thumb:
#   1. If a script can regenerate it, don't commit it.
#   2. If it's a password or key, never commit it - once committed it lives in the
#      history forever, even if you delete the file later.
# =====================================================================================

# --- Large data caches (raw API responses; ~32MB and growing) -------------------------
# Always rebuildable with: python scripts/refresh_all.py --force
data/cache/

# --- Secrets --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This system needs NO API keys. If you ever add one (e.g. FRED_API_KEY), put it in a
# .env file - never paste it into a Python file.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem
credentials.json
secrets.json
*_secret*
*_token*

# --- Python ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# --- OS / editor / OneDrive noise ------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
~$*
*.tmp
.vscode/
.idea/

# =====================================================================================
# WHAT IS DELIBERATELY **NOT** IGNORED - and why
#
#   memory/     the prediction record and lessons learned
#   reports/    the digests
#   research/   the written theses
#   data/       everything except the cache
#
# CLAUDE.md requires the historical record of what was believed, and when, to be
# preserved and un-rewritable. Ignoring those folders would defeat the whole point of
# version-controlling this project.
# =====================================================================================
